OL,3,GNEWSACampaigners say river bacteria
OL,4,Alevels too high
OL,5,
OL,6,FCampaigners have called for action to
OL,7,Fbe taken after discovering bacteria
OL,8,Flevels in a York river were "well and
OL,9,Ftruly above satisfactory".
OL,11,FFor the past five months, members of
OL,12,Fthe Ouse It or Lose It group have
OL,13,Fgathered weekly water samples from the
OL,14,FRiver Ouse to test for bacteria and
OL,15,Fpollutants.
OL,17,FThe group, which tests for four kinds
OL,18,Fof bacteria including E. coli, said
OL,19,Fpolluted rivers could not be accepted
OL,20,Fas "inevitable" and called for greater
OL,21,Ftransparency from those responsible for
OL,22,Flocal rivers.
OL,23,APub: 26-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
